<title>CANADA: ATS plans two-for-one stock split.</title>
<headline>ATS plans two-for-one stock split.</headline>
<dateline>CAMBRIDGE, Ontario 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>ATS Automation Tooling Systems said on Monday it planned to split its common shares on a two-for-one basis and cancel its convertible shares, none of which was issued or outstanding.</p>
<p>The company said it expected the stock split to occur around mid-December, after it held a special shareholders meeting on November 27 to approve the resolutions.</p>
<p>ATS was unchanged at 41.50 in early afternoon trading on the Toronto Stock Exchange.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100</p>
